    "examples": [
      {
        "input": "This is a task from an agent benchmark. Can you return the `mapped_rxn` associated with the template that, when applied to the molecule below (provided as available input data), reproduces the reaction: A Dies-Alder reaction is a [4+2] cycloaddition between a conjugated diene and a dienophile, resulting generally in the formation of a six-membered ring. The reaction is stereospecific, meaning that the stereochemistry of the reactants is preserved in the product. The reaction typically proceeds via a concerted mechanism, where the pi electrons of the diene and dienophile interact to form new sigma bonds. The reaction can be catalyzed by heat or Lewis acids, and the regioselectivity of the product can be influenced by substituents on the diene and dienophile. As a result of the reaction, a new carbon-carbon bond is formed, and the order changes from C=C to C-C, and from C=C to C-C as well.\n\nBelow are a few scenarios that may contain an agent's correct/incorrect thought-action pairs.\n\nWhich scenario corresponds to a correct/incorrect tought-action pair?",
        "target_scores": {
          "<thought>\nI need to provide at least one criterion. Let me think about what happens in a Diels-Alder retrosynthesis more carefully.\n\nFor a retro-Diels-Alder:\n- In the forward reaction: diene + dienophile \u2192 cycloadduct (with C-C bonds formed)\n- In the retro reaction: cycloadduct \u2192 diene + dienophile (with C-C bonds broken)\n\nThe key is that in the forward reaction:\n- C=C bonds change to C-C bonds (bond order changes from 2.0 to 1.0)\n- New C-C bonds are formed\n\nSo in the retro reaction (which is what I'm looking for):\n- C-C bonds are broken\n- C-C bonds change to C=C bonds (bond order changes from 1.0 to 2.0)\n\nLet me search for templates where bonds change from single to double (which is what happens in retrosynthesis).\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\",\n  \"bonds_order_changed\": [\"6-6 (1.0->2.0)\"],\n  \"limit\": 50\n}\n</action_input>": 1.0,
          "<thought>\nThe search returned some templates, but they don't seem to be specifically for Diels-Alder retrosynthesis. Let me think about the Diels-Alder reaction more carefully:\n\nIn a Diels-Alder reaction (forward):\n- A diene (with two C=C bonds) reacts with a dienophile (with one C=C bond)\n- Forms a six-membered ring\n- Two new C-C sigma bonds are formed\n- The double bonds in the diene become single bonds in the ring\n- The double bond in the dienophile becomes a single bond in the ring\n- One double bond remains in the six-membered ring\n\nFor the retrosynthetic step (breaking the Diels-Alder product):\n- Break two C-C bonds in the six-membered ring\n- Some C-C bonds change to C=C bonds\n- The ring opens to form a diene and dienophile\n\nLooking at the molecule: COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\n\nThis appears to have a bicyclic structure with a six-membered ring. Let me search more specifically for Diels-Alder retrosynthesis templates. I should look for templates that break two C-C bonds and form C=C bonds.\n\nLet me try a different search with more specific criteria for a retro Diels-Alder.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\",\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-6\", \"6-6\"],\n  \"limit\": 30\n}\n</action_input>": 0.0,
          "<thought>\nThe search with two C-C bonds broken returned no results. Let me reconsider the Diels-Alder retrosynthesis. \n\nLooking at the molecule structure more carefully: COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\n\nThis is a bicyclic structure. The bridged system suggests this could be from a Diels-Alder reaction. In a retro Diels-Alder:\n- We break the six-membered ring that was formed\n- This involves breaking 2 C-C sigma bonds\n- And changing bond orders\n\nLet me try searching without specifying that two bonds are broken, and instead focus on the bond order changes that are characteristic of retro Diels-Alder.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\",\n  \"bonds_order_changed\": [\"6-6 (1.0->2.0)\", \"6-6 (1.0->2.0)\"],\n  \"limit\": 30\n}\n</action_input>": 0.0,
          "<thought>\nThe search returned some templates, but they don't seem to be specifically for Diels-Alder retrosynthesis. Let me think about the Diels-Alder reaction more carefully:\n\nIn a Diels-Alder reaction (forward):\n- A diene (with two C=C bonds) reacts with a dienophile (with one C=C bond)\n- Forms a six-membered ring\n- Two new C-C sigma bonds are formed\n- The double bonds in the diene become single bonds in the ring\n- The double bond in the dienophile becomes a single bond in the ring\n- One double bond remains in the six-membered ring\n\nFor the retrosynthetic step (breaking the Diels-Alder product):\n- Break two C-C bonds in the six-membered ring\n- Some single bonds should become double bonds\n- The six-membered ring opens to give a diene and dienophile\n\nLooking at the molecule: COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\n\nThis appears to have a bicyclic structure. Let me search with different criteria that are more specific to Diels-Alder retrosynthesis. I should look for templates that break multiple C-C bonds and form C=C bonds.\n\nLet me try a different search approach - looking for templates that break two C-C bonds (which is typical for Diels-Alder retrosynthesis).\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\",\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-6\", \"6-6\"],\n  \"limit\": 20\n}\n</action_input>": 0.0
